WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.140
Speaker 1: So to recap, the Macron variant
is now wreaking havoc throughout the U.S.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:09.889
and the rest of the world, and we're now seeing
at least 100000 new cases of COVID every single

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:13.259
day here in the U.S., with estimates showing
that it could get a lot worse.

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.990
But there are some people suggesting that
there's no reason to worry because yes, while

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.000
Macron is quite contagious and we may see
a lot of infections, it's not going to be

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.320
very deadly.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.510
We're not going to see a big spike in the
death numbers.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:29.800
And the evidence that people base that off
of is the fact that we have this data out

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.480
of South Africa where the variant is believed
to have originated, and it just wasn't all

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.580
that deadly there.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.890
Well, there's this great piece now in NPR
highlighting that what we saw in South Africa

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.160
may not exactly match up with what we're going
to see here in the U.S.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.000
We certainly hope that it does.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.640
We certainly hope that there's not this big
spike in the death numbers, but we just we

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.100
don't know for sure we can't exactly bank
on that.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.720
A study out of South Africa with 200000 COVID
positive participants, about a quarter of

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:02.590
whom had serious underlying health conditions,
was underway between September and November

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:03.590
of this year.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:08.080
So that's the tail end of the delta wave,
along with the beginning of the al-Muqrin

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.080
wave.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.210
Researchers found that as time went on and
al-Muqrin became dominant, there was a 30

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.410
percent drop in hospitalizations from this
pool of people with the COVID cases.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:22.280
The rate of hospitalization for all Macron
was quite low as only 58 per 1000, which is

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.840
the lowest of the four COVID waves that the
country has experienced since this all started

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:27.840
two years ago.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.420
Hard to believe it's been that long.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:35.080
Not only that, instances of patients needing
oxygen or ventilation dropped and ICU stays

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.010
went down to only 13 percent from where it
was at, at 30 percent.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:42.830
Also, people recovered a lot quicker than
in the previous waves.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:43.830
So there you go, right?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.240
We're going to be just fine here.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.920
Well, maybe let's let's hold our horses here
because the key variable is that the data

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.390
did not take into account previous exposure
to the virus.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.850
And many of these cases were reinfections,
with South Africa believed to have a much

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.840
higher level of immunity than we have here
in the United States.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.490
Now the vaccination rates in South Africa,
they're quite a bit lower.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.619
Only about one in four South Africans had
been vaccinated by the time that al-Muqrin

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:10.619
hit.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:15.340
But the vast majority of residents in South
Africa had so-called natural immunity, having

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.730
had a previous version of coronavirus.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:23.950
So between previous infections and the amount
of people who are vaccinated in South Africa,

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:29.080
there were just few people statistically left
who hadn't been exposed to either the virus

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.890
or the vaccine.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:35.310
Nearly everyone in this COVID pool that they
looked at had some version of immunity.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.580
And we know that when you get COVID for a
second time or when you get it after having

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.290
been vaccinated, symptoms aren't nearly as
bad.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:47.680
The death counts aren't nearly as bad, and
your recovery time is generally a lot quicker.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.940
So key to understanding this may be to figure
out the number of people in the U.S. with

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:56.020
no previous exposure to COVID or the vaccine,
and we'll have to see.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.500
We'll have to wait and see how this is going
to affect them.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.500
As of now, about 62 percent of Americans have
been vaccinated, fully vaccinated with the

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.290
two doses, and an estimated 20 percent of
Americans have been infected with COVID since

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:10.290
the start of the pandemic.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.540
It's hard to believe it's only 20 percent.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.170
You'd think it'd be a lot higher than that
number.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.140
Now, obviously, there's going to be some crossover
between these two groups of people because

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.330
some people got vaccinated and then later
got a breakthrough case of COVID.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.090
There's also people who got COVID early on
and then later got vaccinated.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:29.120
So you can't just like, add up the two numbers
and come up with your overall immunity number.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.739
But when you actually crunched the numbers,
when you do it appropriately, it turns out

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:38.500
that 20 percent of Americans, that's 66 million
people have no immunity at all.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:42.190
And that leaves plenty of people who could
potentially get a serious case, depending

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:44.060
really on how severe all Macron is.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.560
And again, we just don't know yet, so we can
be optimistic about the variant.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.750
But we have to be cautiously optimistic, and
the best way to do that is to obviously observe

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.440
the normal protocols.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.120
Wear the mask, socially distance, get vaccinated.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.060
If you're eligible, get the booster shot,
if you can.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:03.250
I just got my booster shot a couple of days
ago wasn't feeling so great yesterday, but

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.930
you know, I got over the side effects in about
a day or so.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.430
Do all the right things.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:12.830
Make sure that we don't just throw caution
to the wind here and make sure that we observe

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:13.860
the right protocols.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:17.609
And hopefully Omicron doesn't turn out to
be so bad, but we just don't know for sure

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:18.609
yet.

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:19.609
We're going to go to a break.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:21.650
We'll be back with much, much more on the
David Pakman show right after this.

